course: dictionary
lesson: 11011
title: Waterline
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A waterline is the line on the side of a boat or ship where the water reaches. The word is made of two words: water and line.
explain: «If the ship pushes aside water that weighs as much as the whole ship before its deck reaches the waterline, it floats.» Here the waterline is a place on the ship's side, not a line drawn on the sea. Ask yourself: what does the sentence say about the ship and the water? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Waterline can also mean a mark that shows how high water has come, such as on a wall after a flood or on a beach. Phrases help too: "below the waterline" means under that mark, and "above the waterline" means higher than it.
fact: Waterline is a noun: the waterline, waterlines.
fact: A waterline is where the water reaches on the side of a ship or boat.
fact: After a flood, a waterline on a wall shows how deep the water was.
fact: "Below the waterline" means under the water mark; "above the waterline" means higher than it.
fact: In science, a boat that carries more weight sits lower in the water, so its waterline climbs higher up its side.
exercise: In «before its deck reaches the waterline», what is the waterline? | *The line on the side of the ship where the water reaches | A rope tied to the anchor | The bottom of the sea | The top of the mast
exercise: After the flood, a line on the wall showed how high the water had come. What is that line called? | Rooftop | *Waterline | Skyline | Doorstep
exercise: A boat carries a heavy load and sits lower in the water. What happens to its waterline? | *It climbs higher up the side of the boat | It stays exactly the same | It disappears
test: Which phrase means higher than the water mark? | Below the waterline | Beside the waterline | Under the waterline | *Above the waterline
test: What does a mark on a wall after a flood show? | How cold the water was | Where the birds nest | When the rain started | *How high the water came
exam: «If the ship pushes aside water that weighs as much as the whole ship before its deck reaches the waterline, it floats.» What does waterline mean here? | *The line on the ship's side where the water reaches | The speed of the ship | The colour of the sea | The number of sailors
